Basic Slicing Examples
For s = "hello":
s[0:3] gets "hel" (from index 0 up to but not including 3).
s[:3] gets "hel" (omitting start defaults to 0).
s[2:] gets "llo" (omitting stop goes to end).

Negative Indices
Negative indices count from the end (-1 is last character):
s[-3:] gets "llo" (last three characters).
s[:-3] gets "he" (up to third-from-end, excluding it).
s[-3:0:-1] gets "lle" (from third-last backward to first, excluding 0).
​

Step Examples
s[::2] gets "hlo" (every second character).
s[1:5:2] gets "el" (from index 1 to 5, every second).
s[::-1] gets "olleh" (full reverse; omit start/stop, use step -1).
​Reverse:
Your original s[0::-1] only gets "h" because starting at 0 with backward step can't go further left.
